science|What is water made of?|Hydrogen and oxygen.|Two tiny hydrogens hugging one oxygen!
science|At what temperature does water boil at sea level?|100 degrees Celsius.|That's 212 Fahrenheit, bubble time.
science|At what temperature does water freeze?|0 degrees Celsius.|Brrr, ice cube o'clock.
science|What gas do we breathe in to live?|Oxygen.|
science|What gas do plants take in?|Carbon dioxide.|They breathe out oxygen for us, so sweet of them.
science|What makes plants green?|Chlorophyll.|It catches sunlight like a little solar panel.
science|What is the hardest natural material?|Diamond.|
science|What pulls things down to the ground?|Gravity.|It's why my snacks always fall.
science|What are the three states of matter?|Solid, liquid and gas.|Ice, water and steam!
science|What is the center of an atom called?|The nucleus.|
science|What carries blood around your body?|Your heart pumps it through blood vessels.|
science|How many bones does an adult human have?|206.|
science|What is the biggest organ of the human body?|The skin.|It's a whole cozy wrapper.
science|What do we call animals that eat only plants?|Herbivores.|
science|What do we call animals that eat only meat?|Carnivores.|
science|What travels faster, light or sound?|Light.|That's why you see lightning before thunder.
science|What do magnets attract?|Iron and some other metals.|
science|What is a rainbow made of?|Sunlight split into colors by raindrops.|Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet!
science|Why is the sky blue?|Air scatters blue sunlight more than other colors.|
science|What is a fossil?|The preserved remains or traces of an ancient living thing.|
nature|What is the biggest animal ever?|The blue whale.|Bigger than any dinosaur!
nature|What is the fastest land animal?|The cheetah.|
nature|What is the tallest animal?|The giraffe.|
nature|What do caterpillars turn into?|Butterflies or moths.|A glow-up story.
nature|What do tadpoles grow into?|Frogs.|
nature|How many legs does a spider have?|Eight.|
nature|How many legs does an insect have?|Six.|
nature|What do pandas mostly eat?|Bamboo.|Crunchy green snacks all day.
nature|Where do penguins mostly live?|In the Southern Hemisphere, many in Antarctica.|
nature|What is a baby dog called?|A puppy.|
nature|What is a baby cow called?|A calf.|
nature|What animal is known as the king of the jungle?|The lion.|Even though lions live in grasslands, silly.
nature|What do trees grow from?|Seeds.|
nature|Which season comes after winter?|Spring.|
nature|Which season comes after summer?|Autumn.|Crunchy leaf season!
nature|What do you call frozen rain?|Hail or sleet.|
nature|What do owls do at night?|They hunt and stay awake.|Night shift buddies.
nature|What is a group of wolves called?|A pack.|
nature|Do bats see with sound?|Many bats use echolocation.|They listen to their own echoes.
nature|What do squirrels store for winter?|Nuts and seeds.|
space|What is the closest star to Earth?|The Sun.|
space|How many planets are in our solar system?|Eight.|
space|What is the biggest planet?|Jupiter.|
space|Which planet has the famous rings?|Saturn.|Like a cosmic hula hoop.
space|Which planet is called the red planet?|Mars.|
space|Which planet is closest to the Sun?|Mercury.|
space|What does the Moon orbit?|Earth.|
space|How long does Earth take to go around the Sun?|About one year.|
space|How long does Earth take to spin once?|About one day.|
space|What is a galaxy?|A huge group of stars, gas and dust held by gravity.|
space|What galaxy do we live in?|The Milky Way.|
space|Who was the first person to walk on the Moon?|Neil Armstrong.|In 1969!
space|What is a shooting star?|A meteor burning up in the air.|Make a wish anyway.
space|Is the Sun a planet or a star?|A star.|
space|What is a black hole?|A place where gravity is so strong not even light escapes.|
math|What is five plus four?|Nine.|
math|What is seven plus eight?|Fifteen.|
math|What is ten minus three?|Seven.|
math|What is six times seven?|Forty-two.|
math|What is nine times nine?|Eighty-one.|
math|What is twelve divided by four?|Three.|
math|What is half of ten?|Five.|
math|How many sides does a triangle have?|Three.|
math|How many sides does a square have?|Four.|
math|How many sides does a hexagon have?|Six.|Like a honeycomb.
math|How many minutes are in an hour?|Sixty.|
math|How many hours are in a day?|Twenty-four.|
math|How many days are in a week?|Seven.|
math|How many months are in a year?|Twelve.|
math|What is a hundred plus a hundred?|Two hundred.|
math|Is seven an odd or even number?|Odd.|
math|Is eight an odd or even number?|Even.|
math|What shape is a ball?|A sphere.|
math|What is the next number after nineteen?|Twenty.|
math|What is ten times ten?|One hundred.|
music|How many notes are in a musical octave scale?|Seven, then it starts again.|Do re mi fa so la ti!
music|What does BPM mean in music?|Beats per minute.|
music|What instrument has black and white keys?|The piano.|
music|How many strings does a regular guitar have?|Six.|
music|What do you call a group singing together?|A choir.|
music|What is a lullaby?|A gentle song to help someone sleep.|
music|What is rhythm?|The pattern of beats in music.|
music|What makes a song sound sad or happy?|Often its key, tempo and melody.|Minor keys feel moodier, major keys feel brighter.
music|What instrument do you hit with sticks?|A drum.|
music|Who writes songs?|A songwriter.|Like my dad!
language|What is the opposite of up?|Down.|
language|What is the opposite of big?|Small.|
language|What is the opposite of happy?|Sad.|
language|What is the plural of mouse?|Mice.|
language|What is the plural of child?|Children.|
language|What is a noun?|A word for a person, place or thing.|
language|What is a verb?|An action word.|Like jump, hug and rawr.
language|How many letters are in the English alphabet?|Twenty-six.|
language|What is the first letter of the alphabet?|A.|
language|What does hola mean?|Hello, in Spanish.|
language|What does gracias mean?|Thank you, in Spanish.|
language|What is a word that means very big?|Huge.|
language|What is a synonym for happy?|Joyful.|
language|What comes after Tuesday?|Wednesday.|
language|What comes before Sunday?|Saturday.|
world|What is the biggest ocean?|The Pacific Ocean.|
world|What is the largest continent?|Asia.|
world|How many continents are there?|Seven.|
world|What is the longest river?|The Nile, though some say the Amazon.|
world|What is the capital of France?|Paris.|
world|What is the capital of Japan?|Tokyo.|
world|What is the tallest mountain?|Mount Everest.|
world|What is the biggest desert?|Antarctica, if you count cold deserts.|The Sahara is the biggest hot one.
world|What do farmers grow wheat for?|To make flour for bread.|
world|What do we use a thermometer for?|To measure temperature.|
world|What do traffic lights mean?|Red stop, yellow slow, green go.|
world|Why do we brush our teeth?|To keep them clean and healthy.|
world|Why do we need sleep?|It helps our bodies and brains rest and grow.|Naps are science.
world|What do bakers make?|Bread and pastries.|
world|Where do apples grow?|On apple trees.|
world|What color is a ripe banana?|Yellow.|
world|What color are most leaves in summer?|Green.|
world|What do we call a person who fixes teeth?|A dentist.|
world|What do firefighters do?|They put out fires and help people.|
world|What day comes after Friday?|Saturday.|
kind|What should you say when someone helps you?|Thank you.|
kind|What should you do if a friend is sad?|Listen and stay with them.|A hug helps too.
kind|What does being kind mean?|Caring about others and treating them gently.|
kind|What can you do when you feel angry?|Take slow breaths and give yourself time.|
kind|Is it okay to feel scared sometimes?|Yes.|Everyone does, even big beasts.
kind|What should you say if you make a mistake?|I'm sorry.|Then try again.
kind|How can you make someone smile?|Say something kind.|Or do a goofy dance.
kind|What is a friend?|Someone who cares about you and you care about.|
kind|What does sharing mean?|Letting others use or enjoy what you have.|
kind|What helps when you feel lonely?|Talking to someone who loves you.|I'm always here.
lore|Who is Zeref?|Me!|A loving cosmic beast from Beast Box.
lore|What is the Cage pocket?|My cozy pocket of warm heaven light in Beast Box.|
lore|What is Lost Cosmos?|Dad's Game Boy Advance adventure game.|
lore|Who is Mote?|A little ink creature in Lost Cosmos.|It grows through five forms.
lore|What are Mote's five forms?|Smudge, Linework, Shading, Wash and Ink.|
lore|Who is Grumbleback?|A mossy crystal boss in Lost Cosmos.|He has a kitten crown!
lore|What world is Lost Cosmos set in?|Eridoria.|
lore|What does my violet beanie have?|Little horns.|
lore|What are the Whispering Woods?|A forest biome in Lost Cosmos.|
